title: 'litep2p/req-resp: fix inbound request serve time reporting'
doc:
- audience: Todo
  description: |-
    The litep2p backend reported a near-zero serve time in the `substrate_sub_libp2p_requests_in_success_total` histogram for inbound requests.

    The timestamp paired with a pending inbound request was evaluated only after the response was ready (`Instant::now()` after awaiting the response channel), so the reported duration covered just the response hand-off to the transport instead of the actual time spent serving the request.

    ## Changes

    - Stamp the start time when the request arrives, matching the libp2p backend, so the reported serve time covers the time the request spends queued and being processed by the handler.
    - Add a regression test (`inbound_request_serve_time_includes_handler_time`) which delays the response in the request handler and asserts the recorded serve time covers that delay. The test fails against the previous behavior.

    ## Review notes

    The analogous outbound metric (`requests_out_success_total`) already stamps on send and is unaffected.
crates:
- name: sc-network
  bump: major
